window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-fa2e3549e489b26b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"remediate-a-vulnerability-backlog\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">修复漏洞积压事项</h1> <p>将已审查的发现项转化为小范围修复，并附上回归验证证据。</p> <p>从工单工具或漏洞报告系统导入已批准的发现项，然后使用 Codex Security 插件逐项验证和处理，采用范围明确的补丁并提供回归证据。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要处理已审查发现项的团队；这些发现可能来自 Codex Security、Linear 或 Jira 工单、GitHub Security Advisories、HackerOne 或 Bugcrowd 报告、渗透测试或内部安全审查。</li> <li>每项补丁都需要最小差异和可重复验证的漏洞积压事项。</li> <li>希望将安全修复与较大范围重构或清理任务分开的维护者。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">$codex-security:fix-finding</a></td> <td>使用有针对性的测试或复现证据，修复并验证一项已验证或可能存在的安全问题。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>修复一项已审查的发现</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $codex-security:fix-finding 修复此安全问题，并验证该问题已无法复现。\n\n来源：[Codex Security report / Linear or Jira ticket / GitHub Security Advisory / HackerOne or Bugcrowd report / other authorized source]\n\n标题和受影响组件：[finding title and component]\n\n存在漏洞的 source、sink 或失效的控制措施：[known path or unknown]\n\n攻击者可控的输入及影响：[input, prerequisites, and impact]\n\n预期的安全不变量：[behavior the fix must enforce]\n\n现有证据：[report path, PoC, reproducer, test, or validation notes]\n\n受影响文件和行号：[paths and lines, or unknown]\n\n约束：[supported behavior to preserve, test command, rollout requirement, or none]\n\n要求：\n\n- 可行时，在更改代码之前确认问题仍然存在。\n\n- 采用能够落实预期安全不变量的最小更改。\n\n- 添加有针对性的回归覆盖，或提供当前可用的最强可重复验证制品。\n\n- 验证正常行为仍然有效，并且原问题已无法复现。\n\n- 不要将积压中的其他问题或重构混入本次更改。\n\n请报告变更文件、测试或验证制品、确切命令及结果、证明原问题已无法复现的证据，以及仍存在的不确定性。如果问题已经修复，请展示证据且不要改动代码。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复发现项指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/deep-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">运行深度安全扫描（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">对代码更改进行安全扫描（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"fix-reviewed-findings-one-at-a-time\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">逐项修复经过审查的发现</h2> <p>当某项安全发现已有足够证据，可以据此限定修复范围后，再使用此工作流。发现项可以来自 Codex Security 插件、Linear 或 Jira 等问题跟踪工具、GitHub Security Advisories、HackerOne 或 Bugcrowd 等漏洞披露平台、内部审查，或其他获准的来源。如果有支持的连接方式，请连接来源；否则尽可能提供报告、工单或公告，以及受影响代码和证据。</p> <p>不要把一长串积压问题交给 Codex 并要求它一次性全部更改。逐项处理有助于审查安全不变量、补丁和验证证据。</p> <p><a id=\"close-one-item-with-evidence\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">用证据关闭一项</h2> <ol> <li>从 Codex Security、工单系统、安全公告、漏洞披露平台，或团队授权用于修复的其他来源中选择一项发现。</li> <li>提供或检索该发现的来源引用、漏洞代码或失效的控制措施、攻击者可控的输入、受影响文件、复现证据和预期的安全行为。</li> <li>要求 <code>$codex-security:fix-finding</code> 在生成最小补丁前先复现或验证问题；如果问题已经修复，则报告无需更改代码。</li> <li>同时审查回归测试或验证制品以及补丁。</li> <li>确认正常行为仍受支持，并且原先有漏洞的路径已无法复现。</li> <li>记录仍存在的不确定性，然后再选择下一项。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"keep-the-backlog-auditable\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">让积压记录可审计</h2> <p>对于每项已完成的问题，保留原始工单、公告或报告引用、确切代码更改、运行过的检查及任何证据缺口。如果 Codex 发现问题已经修复或无法复现，应记录这些证据，而不是强行做出不必要的更改。</p> <p>有关发现项工作区和基于提示词的修复流程，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin/fix-findings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复并验证安全发现项（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"remediate-a-vulnerability-backlog\">Remediate a vulnerability backlog</h1> <p>Turn reviewed findings into minimal fixes with regression evidence.</p> <p>Bring in approved findings from ticketing tools or vulnerability reporting systems, then use the Codex Security plugin to validate and address them one at a time with bounded patches and regression evidence.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams with reviewed findings from Codex Security, Linear or Jira tickets, GitHub Security Advisories, HackerOne or Bugcrowd reports, penetration tests, or internal security reviews.</li> <li>Vulnerability backlogs where every patch needs a minimal diff and repeatable validation.</li> <li>Maintainers who want to separate security remediation from broader refactors or cleanup.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">$codex-security:fix-finding</a></td> <td>Fix and verify one validated or plausible security finding with focused tests or reproduction evidence.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Fix One Reviewed Finding</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:fix-finding to fix this security finding and verify the issue no longer reproduces.\n\nSource: [Codex Security report / Linear or Jira ticket / GitHub Security Advisory / HackerOne or Bugcrowd report / other authorized source]\nTitle and affected component: [finding title and component]\nVulnerable source, sink, or broken control: [known path or unknown]\nAttacker-controlled input and impact: [input, prerequisites, and impact]\nExpected security invariant: [behavior the fix must enforce]\nExisting proof: [report path, PoC, reproducer, test, or validation notes]\nAffected files and lines: [paths and lines, or unknown]\nConstraints: [supported behavior to preserve, test command, rollout requirement, or none]\n\nRequirements:\n- Confirm that the issue still exists before changing code when feasible.\n- Make the smallest change that enforces the intended security invariant.\n- Add focused regression coverage or the strongest repeatable validation artifact available.\n- Verify legitimate behavior still works and the original issue no longer reproduces.\n- Keep unrelated backlog findings and refactors out of this change.\n\nReport the changed files, tests or validation artifacts, exact commands and results, proof that the original issue no longer reproduces, and remaining uncertainty. If the issue is already fixed, show the evidence and do not change code.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix-finding guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/deep-security-scan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run a deep security scan (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scan code changes for security (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"fix-reviewed-findings-one-at-a-time\">Fix reviewed findings one at a time</h2> <p>Use this workflow after a security finding has enough evidence for a bounded remediation decision. The finding can come from the Codex Security plugin, an issue tracker such as Linear or Jira, GitHub Security Advisories, a disclosure platform such as HackerOne or Bugcrowd, an internal review, or another authorized source. Connect the source where supported, or provide the report, ticket, or advisory with affected code and evidence whenever possible.</p> <p>Don't hand Codex a broad backlog and ask it to change everything at once. A single-finding loop keeps the security invariant, patch, and validation evidence reviewable.</p> <h2 id=\"close-one-item-with-evidence\">Close one item with evidence</h2> <ol> <li>Select a finding from Codex Security, a ticketing system, a security advisory, a disclosure platform, or another source your team authorizes for remediation.</li> <li>Provide or retrieve its source reference, source or broken control, attacker-controlled input, affected files, reproduction evidence, and intended secure behavior.</li> <li>Ask <code>$codex-security:fix-finding</code> to reproduce or validate the issue before making a minimal patch, or to report that no code change is needed if it is already fixed.</li> <li>Review the regression test or validation artifact alongside the patch.</li> <li>Confirm that legitimate behavior remains supported and that the original vulnerable path no longer reproduces.</li> <li>Record remaining uncertainty before selecting the next item.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"keep-the-backlog-auditable\">Keep the backlog auditable</h2> <p>For each completed item, keep the original ticket, advisory, or report reference; the exact code change; the checks run; and any proof gap. If Codex finds that the issue is already fixed or it can't reproduce it, record that evidence instead of forcing an unnecessary code change.</p> <p>For the findings workspace and prompt-driven remediation paths, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin/fix-findings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fix and verify security findings (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p>"};
